  "source_report": "Navajo remaining scope: all 329 complete canonical values examined, including four long resources and plural text. No arbitrary priority cutoff. /tmp/nv329-scope-review.json records every typed identity, full canonical wording, reason and exact Kotlin references. After successful dictionary retrieval, one short candidate proposed pending independent review: ui_top = ʼAkʼijįʼ (on top), directly from printed p6/PDF13 and actual crop-edge consumer. /tmp/nv-full-author-proposals.json contains this one value. 311 require language validation, 15 technical/numeric/identifier-only entries excluded from authorship counts, two exact-canonical duplicate alias candidates separately in /tmp/nv-reuse-alias-candidates.json. Aliases are not new translation and do not independently certify inherited target wording; both missing aliases have no exact Kotlin consumer. Nothing integrated. All 329 gaps remain open pending review/action.\n\nSources: Wall and Morgan, Navajo-English Dictionary (1958), BIA, metadata directly verified https://digscholarship.unco.edu/navajo/1/ . Direct PDF web tool returned 403. Confirmed primary-document mirror https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6c/Navajo-English_Dictionary.pdf exceeded web size limit, but curl successfully downloaded its 13,301,006 bytes to /tmp/nv-wall-morgan-1958.pdf. pdftotext output /tmp/nv-wall-morgan-1958.txt available; OCR is visibly poor, so typography must be checked on original page before adopting a term. This retrieval is successful, not a remaining infrastructure excuse.\n\nNavajo Language Academy/Swarthmore lexicon hub https://talkingdictionary.swarthmore.edu/navajo/ returned web 502; confirmed source for subsequent direct retrieval. Navajo Nation education resources https://navajonationdode.org/resources/ lists language-learning resources. UNM program https://navajo.unm.edu/books/ lists established grammars/dictionaries, not an app-localization glossary.\n\nAuthored Diné technical terminology project https://ojb-quantum.github.io/Navaho-Linguistics/ by Onri Jay Benally was directly read for provenance and technical examples. Its quantum/hardware scope does not establish image-editor legal, codec or full imperative semantics. Technical coined terms and dictionary roots alone do not justify generating unverified full Navajo sentences.\n\nTIFF: formats22_tiff_description remains explicitly deferred. Existing missingNavajoDescriptionFallsBackToQualifiedEnglishForBothChoices test therefore remains valid. If a later accepted candidate adds it, the missing-locale fixture must be reassessed, not its assertions weakened.\n\nFollow-up completed: all390 inherited values separately read; see nv390-existing-independent-review.json and nv390-existing-review-report.txt, with two unresolved precision issues and no invented full repairs. Missing-value deferral is not a native-language quality judgement or statement translation is impossible, only that proposed full values have not met evidence/competence threshold in this pass.\n",
  "existing_report": "All 390 inherited full values independently read against canonical, separate from all 329 missing. Source context and per-value statuses/refs: nv390-existing-review-context.json and nv390-existing-independent-review.json. Full approved repair proposals: zero. Two actionable semantic-precision issues remain unsolved linguistically, not silently accepted: selected destination reduced to here, and sampled decoding described as opening a smaller copy rather than explicit sampling of source pixels. Their actual consumers and limits are recorded. A competent full Navajo rewrite is needed before integration; no English insertion or guessed inflection supplied.\n\nPrimary dictionary source successfully downloaded and rendered. Wall/Morgan1958, printed p22/PDF29 explicitly confirms biʼoh neelʼą́ insufficient/too little. Render /tmp/nv-dictionary-p29.png. Therefore inherited memory warnings are NOT afflicted by the Quechua no-more-memory defect. Printed p6/PDF13 lists heart-shaped phrase and on-top phrase. Render /tmp/nv-dictionary-p13.png. Heart existing Yaago heeneez was not rejected: linguistic literal decompositions can be misleading. No native certification based on dictionary entries.\n\nActual code refuted several potential false positives: ImageResizeDialog checks 1×1 decoding plan and limits choices to original size; AssemblyRenderer.suggested checks 1×1 before showing floor warning. Downsizing wording and explicit smallest1×1 are supported by these consumers. Unexpected undo-cache error follows additional byte after expected pixel data; detailed Navajo bytes explanation tracks it. No manufactured bulk correction.\n\nTwo canonical-only duplicate alias candidates remain isolated from new substantive translation counts. Their existing target wording is not independently certified by matching English. Long help/legal/codec missing values remain unsupported, not filled with English to inflate presence. No installed-device or layout verification performed. No repository edits.\n\nSwarthmore confirmed hub direct curl also failed HTTP503, following web502. This is reported accurately, but does not negate accessible dictionary evidence. Search roots/technology terms do not supply an authoritative Navajo app-localization glossary or establish full long-clause grammar.\n",
